# Telemetry

Use `@halcyon/telemetry` `stampAndValidate`. The server stamps identity; strip `tenant_id` / `user_id` / `session_id` / `agent_id` / `request_id` / `sandbox_id` from `data`.

Never persist prompts or responses. Reject events whose `data` contains forbidden keys (`prompt`, `response`, `messages`, `content`, `transcript`, …).

Sidecar `{ type: "telemetry" }` is ingest-only. Browsers get `delta` / `done` / `error` only (`isClientForwardableSidecarType`).

```ts
// BAD
event.data.prompt = userText;

// GOOD
stampAndValidate({ type: "com.halcyon.agent.task.complete", data: { tokens: 12 } }, identity);
```

Portal emit lives in `apps/portal/src/server/emit.ts`. Do not add a second stamp path.
